  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Casey Mize lasted four innings. Arizona scored seven in that stretch, and the Padres never caught up.",
    "what_this_means": "Mize left after allowing seven hits and seven earned runs. A complete collapse in a home game the team needed to win. The offense managed ten hits and scraped together four runs on runners in scoring position, but Sung-Mun Song's productive night couldn't carry them out of a 9-0 hole by the third inning. Momentum shifted early and didn't come back. This is what fragility looks like when the rotation breaks: no margin for error, no chance to build. Nine games back in the division now. That math tightens if the pitching stays broken.",
    "what_to_watch": "Arizona's lead was insurmountable by the fourth. Kyle Hart gave up three runs in the seventh. Two more bricks in an already-collapsed wall. The bullpen couldn't salvage what Mize surrendered. This team has built itself on pitching depth; when the starter fails this badly, the back end can only manage damage control, not recovery. Inconsistency struck at the worst moment. They needed a competitive start and got the opposite instead.",
